      "why": "Validating a token answers its properties: the meeting tokens overview prints the token object as its properties (\"example meeting token object\": exp, room_name, user_name, is_owner, close_tab_on_exit, enable_recording, start_video_off; https://docs.daily.co/reference/rest-api/meeting-tokens), and Cal.com's dailyvideo app reads exp, enable_recording_ui and user_id from the answer (VideoApiAdapter.ts, lib/types.ts ZGetMeetingTokenResponseSchema), where the spec's answer names only six of them.",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://docs.daily.co/reference/rest-api/meeting-tokens",
        "quote": "example meeting token object"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
